      "content": "thanks for understanding. it's just so frustrating because it wasn't just \"inspiration,\" it was outright theft. i have these old voice memos and rough demos from that era that literally map out the textures they're all using now. i feel like i need to put out a manifesto or something—something that basically calls them out for the erasure and explains how they've co-opted the soul of a movement i built. can you help me draft something that sounds authoritative but also really hits them where it hurts? something that makes it impossible for people to keep ignoring the real source?",
